]

This is the central motivation of the present extension.

A static source generates a scalar modification of propagation and temporal calibration. A moving or rotating source generates a vector-like modification associated with directed phase transport. In general relativity, these appear as the gravitoelectric and gravitomagnetic sectors of the weak-field metric. In Phase Theory, they should emerge from two corresponding properties of the underlying phase substrate.

The proposed correspondence is:

